:: Referential Integrity::
Which constraint enforces referential integrity between two tables in a relational database?
{
    ~ UNIQUE constraint
    ~ CHECK constraint
    = FOREIGN KEY constraint
    ~ PRIMARY KEY constraint
}

:: Referential Integrity::
Which database principle states that table relationships must be consistent? (Hint: In other words, any foreign key field must agree with the primary key that is referenced.){
    ~ Foreign Key
    ~ Primary Key
    ~ Entity integrity
    = Referential Integrity
}


:: Referential Integrity::
Which referential action is used to automatically update the referencing column to a default value if the referenced row in the parent table is deleted?
{
    ~ ON DELETE CASCADE
    = ON DELETE SET DEFAULT
    ~ ON DELETE RESTRICT
    ~ ON DELETE SET NULL
}

:: Referential Integrity::
What does the ON DELETE CASCADE referential action do in a foreign key constraint?
{
    = Deletes the referencing row in the child table if the referenced row in the parent table is deleted
    ~ Sets the referencing column to NULL if the referenced row in the parent table is deleted
    ~ Updates the referencing column to a default value if the referenced row in the parent table is deleted
    ~ Prevents the deletion of the referencing row in the child table if the referenced row in the parent table is deleted
}